  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, not all menus in the action menu act alike. In most sub-menus, the 12 o' clock area is the back button. However, in puppet menus, the back button is the neutral position of the joystick (or take your finger off the trackpad) + trigger to back out of the menu. \nTo make sure this is never ambiguous, leaving a menu/going to a previous menu should always be to put the joystick or trackpad in a neutral position and clicking the trigger. This would also free up an extra spot for users to put additional menu items in as they see fit.",
